<title>BELGIUM: EU says surprised by US grain complaint to WTO.</title>
<headline>EU says surprised by US grain complaint to WTO.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday it was surprised by a complaint from the United States to the World Trade Organisation about its grain import tariff system.</p>
<p>Washington filed the complaint on Friday after losing patience with the EU, notably over rice import rules, following a year of fruitless talks. The main disagreements were over duty free import quotas and cross-subsidisation of imports.</p>
<p>&quot;We are somewhat surprised with the U.S. request as we are still involved in discussions with them on these points,&quot; the Commission's agriculture spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said further technical talks were planned.</p>
<p>The WTO's Dispute Settlement Body is due on December 3 to set up a panel to investigate the U.S. complaint.</p>
</text>
